    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 10 with a lineup anchored by two elite offensive plays against a soft matchup. **Trea Turner** (79.74) leads the team, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and an advantageous matchup against Sugano; his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in the scarcity-heavy stolen base category. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (75.71) is a mandatory start in the same contest, as he leverages strong park factors and the favorable SP_xERA of 4.73 to provide significant power upside. We also see high-ceiling potential from **Junior Caminero** (64.83), who overcomes a tough matchup against Tolle by capitalizing on favorable wind conditions and a high-leverage #2 spot in the order, pushing his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nTactically, we are banking on **Caleb Durbin** (61.18) to provide sneaky value; despite hitting 9th, his score is bolstered by a favorable wind and an advantageous SP_xERA against Martinez. Conversely, the toughest call today was keeping **Carson Benge** (50.21) on the bench. While his 15% SP Skill bonus against Rodriguez made him a viable candidate, he was edged out by the superior platoon alignment of **Dillon Dingler** (60.99) and the consistent profile of our current OF depth. We remain cautious regarding **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (51.39); while his dynamic platoon edge is high, facing deGrom remains a significant risk factor that suppressed his ceiling. We continue to monitor the status of **Zac Veen**, currently rostered but relegated to the minors, and **Christian Yelich**, who remains unavailable on the IL, while keeping a close watch on the lineup pending status for **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** to ensure our projected efficiencies hold through first pitch.",
